nt_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "d0dfc512-8794-4a05-afdb-ec03d1e55710", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "style.\n\nRead on for tips and techniques for constructing Standalone illustrations. This will ensure we're all adhering to the same approved\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:77dce036-43ed-4880-a4fb-53af40aba888"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:4d0187ae-07df-4460-8834-6ba9f35887e4", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "bu!z!s", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "4d0187ae-07df-4460-8834-6ba9f35887e4", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "Standalone illustrations are designed with a canvas size of 200 x 200 px. The longer side of the illustration must measure precisely 200 px, and the ilustration should be centered within the frame. You can scale the illustration while preserving the same proportions as the original 200 x 200 px artwork.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:0695835c-bb36-4edf-b9ea-8342653c8ace"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:8dd608a3-8ac9-4100-81ca-5a10965a70fa", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Bodyshape", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "8dd608a3-8ac9-4100-81ca-5a10965a70fa", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "'sewjue labe o aldoad jo Apog mnt au apnjxa am 'suoensn ano ueap jo jaal pue as iensi suasisuos e ueuie oi Don'tillustrate the fullbody of people or larger animals.\n\nOnly depict the face of larger subjects.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:02e717a6-a249-47df-ad63-ab1d83aae1e1"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:85a4c8ee-9775-4519-9d80-4d3db388e286", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Stroke", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 14, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "85a4c8ee-9775-4519-9d80-4d3db388e286", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "d ' o yrpim aos au ias pue peoge xd ox ooe ym ug im aos woune ym sioans penpu aei\n\n'saos au u saenha lo sdunq neneuun ue jo pionap uealo sheadde uome leu au pue roows ae suod sooan eue Strokefeatures The corners and caps of the strokes should always have rounded attributes.\n\nStrokewidth Don't mix stroke widths in an illustration.\n\nThe stroke width remains at 1.5 pt with a consistent width profile.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:ce00a027-665a-40cf-9563-d75a5d5591d0"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:07fb5b9d-4405-4865-8606-b12081edc1c1", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "07fb5b9d-4405-4865-8606-b12081edc1c1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:fdbee5ef-f00f-4040-9d86-491c8318b6d0"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:741ea0b7-ddcb-4399-a444-9898875e0799", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "FilledAreas", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "741ea0b7-ddcb-4399-a444-9898875e0799", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "ot suoesnlnt au jo t-s uasaida pinoys seaie asaui seaie pa ot dn aney pnous auoepues ay jo sed aos 'suoesnl eu ssooe Aouaisisuos ansua ot pue seaie pa pue sauno uaamaq aouejeq poob e uuiu The filled area must not exceed 15% of the illustration.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:b4d51add-9408-46b8-9e22-5a1467f76a19"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:728cb0c3-de19-4c29-93d0-23445acdac99", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Crossing lines", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 15, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "728cb0c3-de19-4c29-93d0-23445acdac99", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "When suitable for the illustration, employ a 'crossing line' to enhance it. This method involves incorporating an organic line that intersects the artwork, adding dynamism and engagement.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:fcc2f2d5-55dc-4f0f-a808-72f2fcd1089d"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:0f474544-c29f-4f45-877c-9821b537c4a9", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "0f474544-c29f-4f45-877c-9821b537c4a9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\nHuman eye For human eyes, we emphasize detail when rendering the upper eyelid and eyeball. The shape of the upper eyelid may vary based\n\n'suoissaidxa neoe ades ot sn smoe smoaa bupnourae se yns seap peuope auoo sdiay adeys pa laddn a Eyebrows UpperEyelidShape Glasses If a person depicted in the illustration wears glasses, don't draw eyebrows.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:78ad4562-e37b-4af7-8444-0872880be02b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:3a10d39b-db2d-4aa0-b528-f15ae07d27e1", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Animaleyes", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "3a10d39b-db2d-4aa0-b528-f15ae07d27e1", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:eafb3b94-97ea-441e-94a8-d8617da3012c", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Color combination", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 16, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "eafb3b94-97ea-441e-94a8-d8617da3012c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:dc255b81-1327-41f9-be2d-8ef5dcd65a73", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "How to create Scene illustrations", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "dc255b81-1327-41f9-be2d-8ef5dcd65a73", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:dab03006-c3a5-41be-9564-0a6064ad19f3"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:d30f13e6-5c8a-4b12-bf58-ec810ab1028b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Stroke", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "d30f13e6-5c8a-4b12-bf58-ec810ab1028b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "various areas within the illustration, like hands, where they define individual fingers, ensuring enhanced detail.\n\nConsistency is essential in our Scene illustrations, characterized by the use of two consistent stroke widths. Beginning with a 1080 px height artboard, the stroke width is set at 2 pt. While we maintain a handcrafted appearance, it's essential to steer clear of Always ensure vector points are smooth, to deliver a clean, polished final artwork without irregularities in strokes.\n\nBasicstroke The brush stroke adds fine details to hair in both humans and animals. The stroke width is 1 pt, and we use the charcoal pencil available in llustrator. Brushstroke stroke width is 2 pt with a uniform width profile. Corners and caps should consistentlyhaveroundedattributes.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:a4c61646-48ff-43be-bfb6-2a71307451d8"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:e8f8ec81-bcf2-42e2-9123-2a2069f79c21", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Composition", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 17, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "e8f8ec81-bcf2-42e2-9123-2a2069f79c21", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "'saul aoadsiad yonou pahauoo qns aq pinous suauuoua suoesnllul punoyoeq pue punoaiot snleeds aeao o saul aoadsad asn a without the need for intricate detailing. Fullscene relationships within the illustration.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:a9894a91-4f73-4b9b-bc13-60b8f626d0ea"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:81021d5a-a309-46ba-94ff-2cf9828a4b14", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 18, "source_docu