kin Color 06", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:aecbde07-e0f3-4e72-9cc7-aec6e15974d0"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:ddf2500e-ac02-41da-af04-66d77c610023", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Download color swatches for skin tones, shadows and hair", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "ddf2500e-ac02-41da-af04-66d77c610023", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "there's clear contrast between selected colors and refer to the dedicated Color chapter for the correct codes to ensure precise representation.\n\nColor combinationfor clothes examples", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:1150d444-f569-486f-88e8-922578024fa6"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:b00d9d9c-7abf-4102-8a72-032fc21734e6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Color combinations for animals", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 21, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "b00d9d9c-7abf-4102-8a72-032fc21734e6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": ""}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:9fd28a1e-c424-4671-ab46-8f4e892c531b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 22, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "9fd28a1e-c424-4671-ab46-8f4e892c531b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "Furcolors Animal fur colors should align with the primary and secondary palettes, as well as human skin and hair colors when applicable. Choose colorsthat accuratelyreflect thenatural hues of the animals.\n\nExamples of fur colors\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:731cc324-adc6-49ad-bef1-e7bbd395cfd9"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:afbdda13-dd06-419f-ab51-7fe2a0b1b1d9", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "afbdda13-dd06-419f-ab51-7fe2a0b1b1d9", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "Swinecolors Swines should be colored using Skin color 01, 02, 03 (along with their corresponding shadows) from the human skin tone palette.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:b3bf7498-35f7-4936-9271-aa012dd5d618"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:e5f5db49-e0ed-4b2b-9ef1-2e3ac6b4d050", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Eyes andexpression", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "e5f5db49-e0ed-4b2b-9ef1-2e3ac6b4d050", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "Eyes play a central role in our illustrations, vital for showing inclusivity, emotional connections, and expressing feelings.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:7eae6b2b-48c4-4226-92a5-950d9cc5ab93"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:e55459c3-97c1-4ddf-b5b3-4e9956d11513", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Eyesfor humans", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 23, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "e55459c3-97c1-4ddf-b5b3-4e9956d11513", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "Human eyes are illustrated with an emphasis on unique upper eyelid shapes and iris variations to represent different individuals. We complement this with eyebrows to enhance overall facial expressions, evoking relatability and emotional resonance.\n\nShape canforgea deeperconnectionwiththecharactersorsubjects. Expression elongated,rounded,or otherwise,this approach allows us to create diverse and inclusiveillustrations.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:ea7d73b0-3b15-49ee-8510-44122c9524e8"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:b0019e0e-460a-4e52-8535-7aa3a89066da", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "b0019e0e-460a-4e52-8535-7aa3a89066da", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "Eyebrows enhancing the storytelling aspect of ourillustrations.\n\nEyebrows complement the eyes, expanding the range of emotions conveyed and", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:c7898190-020b-4332-9ebd-182c5f4dc791"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:0ef0e04b-9d45-4c04-bd1f-2c7827aab66e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "EyesforAnimals", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "0ef0e04b-9d45-4c04-bd1f-2c7827aab66e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "of emotions through their eyes, harmonizing them with other facial features like the mouth, which fosters a sense of connection and empathybetweenthe audienceand theanimals.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:9f23a972-9cb0-42f1-aeb5-b356adc0599b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:457d8bc2-64e8-4fb7-8097-2330bb2c7a89", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Mouthforhumans", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 24, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "457d8bc2-64e8-4fb7-8097-2330bb2c7a89", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "The mouth, like the eyes, is fundamental for conveying emotions and feelings. We use a simplified representation of lips for both menandwomen.\n\nOpenmouth When we illustrate people talking or smiling,or we want to share a more detailed ofthemouthisblack. age,gender andethnicity. Closedmouth Don't illustrate lips more than this with facial hair-this helps to ensure there aren'ttoomanyelementsintheillustration. Mouthwithbeard When someone is fully smiling we illustrate the internal part of the mouth in white, depicting the teeth without adding too many details. Openmouth-fullteeth Mouthwithmoustache background color.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:bbcdafd3-903c-43dd-86e4-b9e3c26398e7"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:8573b476-f16f-4fd9-baa4-f5043149563c", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 25, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "8573b476-f16f-4fd9-baa4-f5043149563c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "ay urm ljo ayons au useuos pue palun seae aos bueal baes sueau suoensn no jo yadap ay bujouus aysae neiao au bueala usoduoo buebua pue you ens e usnsal pue anaed jojoo au saonpal anbuyoat s dwa uiewa pinus uoesn au o suooas om no auo uo eapi sud peoot o uouae buoap pue ladde\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:fc0b60b3-a9fa-4071-b1f6-a11a16351564"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:9a129ca6-9fd4-42de-9fb4-bc482689ebef", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "How to create Technical illustrations", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 25, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "9a129ca6-9fd4-42de-9fb4-bc482689ebef", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "as paodde anou suesnleyai bueao it sanbuuoan pue saupine ae aiah\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:592fbb49-6b2b-46d5-a074-4343cc5c1731"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:8cbb9d12-4f30-4fc8-85be-26ad6bc886d5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Stroke", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 25, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "8cbb9d12-4f30-4fc8-85be-26ad6bc886d5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "Create the artwork on a 1080 px tall artboard. Use strokes with varying width, ranging from 1 pt to 1.5 pt. These strokes are", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:8ac0c677-8f1b-46f2-bfb1-d8fdf92ee471"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:b388de45-d189-4a5d-9755-0e7f7285d68a", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Organs in animal and human", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "b388de45-d189-4a5d-9755-0e7f7285d68a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "palap aou eaaym sase u uount du pueshaun ue saoune auos seap euassa uo busnot sueio jo suoidap o spuaxa adud s e ases ads au aziseyda o usewu bueuu aum uouoan noagns dt panun Representations of bodies and organs should strike a balance between realism and selective detail. Enough details should be\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:5dcea36f-eedb-4dcb-8c60-f1e378454378"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:57bc703f-4f5b-4ada-8f09-198a26e7c493", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Colorusage", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "57bc703f-4f5b-4ada-8f09-198a26e7c493", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "Colors play a vital role in defining different areas of the illustration. For a more in-depth understanding of our color usage, please refertoLevel O3:Technical.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:b6dd9652-4fb8-41b9-b490-8f45daa8d054"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:9222e3e1-2239-4f9b-8ebd-acb298de0151", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Focuspoint", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 26, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "9222e3e1-2239-4f9b-8ebd-acb298de0151", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "The focus point highlights and emphasizes critical information, guiding the viewer's attention, improving comprehension, and enhancing theoverall educational and aestheticquality oftheillustration.\n\nThe outer circle radius can be adjusted to portray the entire area of interest effectively.\n\noutercircle.\n\nUse'Dark Green'for the inner circle and'Accent Green'at 10% opacity for the uo aseo sads sy ui pamoe s! edo oot yrm uaano zuaooh au jo abesn aui ao", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:16706efd-0024-4ff9-94dc-606052aa54f3"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:b9ab6e75-fffd-4933-9136-ab29de4c5b5b", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Magnifier", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 27, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "b9ab6e75-fffd-4933-9136-ab29de4c5b5b", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "In Technical illustrations, we use magnifiers to offer a closer, more detailed view of the illustration. This helps the audience understand the mechanical aspects and intricacies of the medical subject being depicted.\n\nMagnifiers come in both round and rectangularshapes.\n\nprocesses,enabling the inclusion of additional text as required. Rectangularmagnifier\n\nRoundmagnifier Idealfora close-upview of theillustration,offering aclearer descriptionof the mechanics of the medical topic.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:e640665a-d7df-4937-99ba-77fe8c981fa9"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:2596dc93-facd-41ea-871f-7561a3662c4e", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "r Technical illustrations Examples of our", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 27, "source_document_type": "guidance_document", "section_id": "2596dc93-facd-41ea-871f-7561a3662c4e", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Illustrations 4.pdf", "source_document_id": "ab59869e-f86f-48d4-8916-fb89334732d4", "text": "Pulmonary fibrosis Dog ticks Symptom depictionsMagnifyingtheissue Her2 Tyrosine Kinase Inhibitor Cellularinsight Generalized Pustular Psoriasis (GPP)", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:9a141bca-dba3-4e38-addd-84927669f0cf"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:6f1f2201-d46b-46d7-b0c7-bdd2eb602d37", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Approval of new illustrations", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 27, "source_document_type