howcasesillustrationsthatareemotiveand richindetail.They'reidealfor depictingcomplexscenes and complementing associated headlines.Theseillustrations arenuancedand engage thereaderona deeperlevel,frequently appearingineditorialand digitaltouchpoints.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:b2c75ecf-6e0d-4381-867d-200b5918aa25"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:55c34674-98ef-4deb-bb37-a5281e0b6300", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Colorcombination", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "55c34674-98ef-4deb-bb37-a5281e0b6300", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "InSceneillustrations,wewant to tella storyorcreate aspecific atmosphere.Secondary colors achieve this bygiving us abroaderspectrum of hues.This then helpsus evokespecificemotions and create a playful look andfeel.\n\nWhen changing thecolor,it'sessential thatthebackground seamlesslyintegrateswith the colorsof the\n\nillustration.\n\nAsageneralrule,alwaysselect colorsthatoptimizelegibilityand create a defined contrast.We alsoneed to minimizethedifferenceinvibrancybetweencolors.\n\nHead to the dedicated'Color'chapterforthe correctcolorcodestoensureprecise colorrepresentation.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n\"Warm Gray'background\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nVioletbackground\n\nFromlighttomediumshades\n\nBluebackground Fromlight tomedium shades\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nRed background Fromlighttomediumshades\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPlease ensure thatonlyprofessionals(designers and illustrators) handle comprehensive edits to Sceneillustrations.\n\nNote: Don't use'Dark Green'or'Accent Green'asa background color for Scene illustrations.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:c3eea999-3575-4b8f-b7f4-f7a2a56e5aed"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:5d6d9347-5199-43f1-9900-99bf9599e2a8", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Placement", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "5d6d9347-5199-43f1-9900-99bf9599e2a8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Ourillustrations aredesigned toworkacross differentformats and communicationneeds-sowe canuseit inbothfullbleedandframed.\n\nOfcourse,it'salwaysessentialthattheillustrationremainsclearand easytoidentify.\n\nThe usage ofscenei illustrations withoutbackground isnot allowed.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:4cf4519e-c071-4f2d-9736-347f6020d4fc"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:65b4e568-1a5d-4ea8-9ce3-e799c59c8e7c", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Fullbleedtoframed", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "65b4e568-1a5d-4ea8-9ce3-e799c59c8e7c", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "ASceneillustrationcanbeused infullbleed forflexibilityinthelayout,ortrimmedononeormoresides while aligning with the format'sedges.If framed,makesure theillustrationis clear.\n\nScale and place the illustration\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:cd9e83fe-c4d8-4265-b2ae-5cf2828b60a2"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:cf8e30fe-8e26-4de6-89c5-1e7f4942d164", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Addingadditionalelements", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "cf8e30fe-8e26-4de6-89c5-1e7f4942d164", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "You canscaletheillustration and extend thebackground colortoincorporateadditionalelements.You can inserttextinthisadditionalsection,too.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:40b732e7-bc29-4464-8bc8-7cade9127f6a"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:8f27b7f2-fc96-4e80-ad46-8269e1c44ed3", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Minimum isize", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 7, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8f27b7f2-fc96-4e80-ad46-8269e1c44ed3", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Theminimum sizeofaScene illustration ensuresclearlegibilityandvisibility acrossallphysicaland digital applications.Theminimum sizeis determinedbased on the longersideof theillustration.\n\nminimum screen size\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nminimumprint size\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nTheminimumsizefordigital screensis225pxand theminimumsizeforprintmediais60mm.\n\nExtend thebackground\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nAdd the text\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nYellowbackground From light tomedium shades\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nMagazine\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPowerPoint\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDon'toverlapwith text, imagesorgraphics.\n\nDon'tdistortthe standalonein any way.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDon'toverlapwith otherillustrations.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:4a0f9759-6d49-48cc-a2c5-e60dadaa3a70"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:a5963911-09e7-4f6e-80d6-6436a83d4ec5", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "ILLUSTRATIONS DESIGN GUIDE", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a5963911-09e7-4f6e-80d6-6436a83d4ec5", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:380103b2-5332-495c-a412-8311e35bd5bf"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:a25562c6-dd76-400c-9a4c-fbd009fe4c06", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Sampleapplications", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "a25562c6-dd76-400c-9a4c-fbd009fe4c06", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Use this type ofillustrationwhenyou want toframe a scene or a more specific topic.It helps thereader focusonaparticularaspectorsituation.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nNewsletter\n\nWebsite\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:8c520028-5f53-4aa9-8de2-cd73412b5a68"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:80199423-8aed-4ae2-aa0f-cb716e1e09f0", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Don'ts", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "80199423-8aed-4ae2-aa0f-cb716e1e09f0", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Don't overlapwith text,images orgraphics.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDon't create close-upsof the illustration.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:02a47fa7-7d3b-4600-b880-035c3981022e"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:2dcba660-e482-49cc-aeb3-ebaedfb0f1bf", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Level03:Technical", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2dcba660-e482-49cc-aeb3-ebaedfb0f1bf", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Ourthird level,Technical,featuresthe most detailed and precise illustrations intheset.Theseillustrations preciselyconveycomplexmedicalprocesses and technicalinformation.Weuse themineditorialmaterials andonthewebsite.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nIneachTechnicalillustration,there arethreesub-levelsofdepiction.Eachof themgivesthe audience a unique and clearperspective on themedicalprocessorissue.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nhumans oranimalstoshowcase\n\ndisease symptoms.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:40a9c3aa-9ffd-4fa3-b1b8-efd2e292316f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:85dcd5e5-5be8-42be-baa4-8d312a6f06df", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Colorcombination", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "85dcd5e5-5be8-42be-baa4-8d312a6f06df", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "backgroundsand depictionsofhumansandanimals.\n\nWethenincorporatesecondary colorsto highlightand differentiatevariouselements.These colors representthings slikedifferent typesof diseases or group elements,and create distinctionswithin the illustrations.Thisensures s thatourillustrations aren't justinformative,but are alsovisually organized andeasy tounderstand.\n\nPleaserefer to thededicated'Color'chapterforthecorrectcolor codestoensureprecise color representation.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nSymptom depictionsandmagnifyingtheissue\n\nUse secondary colors exclusively for'Symptom depictions'on animal fur and human clothing. Use white for all otherbodyrepresentations,whether human or animal.\n\nVarious shades of gray are used for depicting the organs,using a darker gray outline for clarity. The specific illnessarea is highlightedwithsecondary colors.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:faa21a10-a488-4351-870d-8e12ae31ea8b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:443c206f-5cae-4bc9-802d-0b07dcd678d7", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Cellularinsights", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "443c206f-5cae-4bc9-802d-0b07dcd678d7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "When depicting different partsof the same organor cellularelement, usevariousshades fromthe secondarypalette.Choose edistincthueswhen differentiation isrequired.\n\nPlease ensure thatonly professionals(designers,illustrators) take careof comprehensive edits to Technicalillustrations", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:0345a890-bfd3-4b11-a149-a9e0b648f87f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:c42d5fb7-a4df-4111-8b25-8e923a589c7a", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Placement", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "c42d5fb7-a4df-4111-8b25-8e923a589c7a", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Technicalillustrations support specificmedical topics.We don't crop the subjects of theseillustrations arbitrarily.However,we'vedesignedvariousformatproportionstocatertodifferentrequirements.\n\nAdditionally,you canadjustthebackground of theillustrationbycropping orextendingit.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nUsingillustrationsin different layouts\n\nCrop thebackground of theillustration\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:d76af101-6540-4c60-b9b9-3cf15e8b3ca7"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:f9953279-0613-4f72-a4e1-a61f2da19319", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Addingadditionalelements", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "f9953279-0613-4f72-a4e1-a61f2da19319", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Use this type ofillustration to convey specificinformation aboutmedical procedures or diseases.It's\n\neffective forpresenting health-related detailsinavisuallyengaging way.\n\nPleased don'tuse theillustrationsfor anytopic thatisunrelated to specificmedical/technical subjects.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:2a43f88e-4efc-4e5b-bdcf-a01976e682a4"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:b5172a6c-7d0f-46b4-be5b-cf640902dfa7", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Sampleapplications", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "b5172a6c-7d0f-46b4-be5b-cf640902dfa7", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "PowerPoint\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:2179e9b9-eb80-4fea-a56b-9e942b8f1912"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:e427ddd6-bcc4-4f29-8289-7d1bbc35377f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Don'ts", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 8, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "e427ddd6-bcc4-4f29-8289-7d1bbc35377f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "<!-- image -->\n\nDon'tuse Technical illustrationsfortopics unrelatedtothe specificmedical subjectthatthe illustrationis describing.\n\nExtend thebackground\n\nAdd the text\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nMagnifying theissue Delving into thehuman or animal body tohighlightinternal medical subjects.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nCellularinsight Revealing intricate medical conceptsbyentering cellsor structurestoprovideadeeper understanding.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nMagazine\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nPowerPoint\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDon'trotate or distortthe illustration.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nAlwaysalign the framed side with the border of the artboard.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDon'toverlapwithtext orimages.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDon't overlap with other illustrations.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nAlways ensure clarity when framing the illustration.\n\nDon'toverlapwith otherillustrations or icons.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nDon'trotateordistort the illustration.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:ecf89332-bb1b-498e-909e-5b79f29e8652"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:0f926125-b564-4bb5-a82c-e45b5659e396", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "0f926125-b564-4bb5-a82c-e45b5659e396", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Boehringer Ingelheim", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:26a946b2-4e0c-4b4d-9d1f-4eb7be6aba92"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:df9b7a7f-24d5-4e9c-903f-3b4590eb53fe", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Illustrationsvs.icons", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "df9b7a7f-24d5-4e9c-903f-3b4590eb53fe", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "When decidingwhether touseanillustration oranicon,remember:weuseillustrationsto conveyvarying degreesofdepth and complexity,evoking amoreemotionalresponse,andadding a storytellingelementto ourdesignandcontent. Weuseiconstosharesimpleinformationandprovideguidanceandnavigation-all throughasingle identifiablegraphic.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:ed3be807-7f27-4496-ba8e-72363b14fb63"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:36fe8e38-6c64-46bc-a5b9-19aa414c31dc", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Creating illustrations", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "36fe8e38-6c64-46bc-a5b9-19aa414c31dc", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "HowtocreatetheStandalone illustrations\n\nReadonfortipsand techniques forconstructing Standalone illustrations.Thiswill ensurewe'realladhering to the same approved style.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:ad1af868-3e40-4b10-b0f7-75f00b4f6ba7"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:1e8a2eea-1104-4d95-8e27-a3344a5465b2", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Sizing", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "1e8a2eea-1104-4d95-8e27-a3344a5465b2", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Standaloneillustrationsaredesignedwithacanvassizeof2o0x200px.Thelongersideof theillustration mustmeasureprecisely2o0px,and theillustration should becentered within the frame.You canscale the illustrationwhilepreservingthesameproportionsastheoriginal2o0x2o0pxartwork.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:c81df635-8774-49e5-8715-7ba0e1875b51"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:d92d983e-2262-4b6f-8028-94b9a3cf5016", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Bodyshape", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "d92d983e-2262-4b6f-8028-94b9a3cf5016", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Tomaintaina consistentvisualstyleand levelofdetailinourillustrations,weexcludethefullbodyofpeople orlargeranimals. Thisguideline appliestoanimalssuchascows,horses,and otherspeciessurpassing specificsizeorweight threshold,typicallymeasuring over7o cminheightattheshoulder. Humansare alwaysportraitstylewiththefaceonly.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:a38cd815-e6ba-41be-be15-7877a1ae7dbf"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:630ea21c-1e5f-4496-9c4a-ad02c9954cf6", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Stroke", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "630ea21c-1e5f-4496-9c4a-ad02c9954cf6", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Createindividualsubjectswithauniformstrokewidth.Beginwitha200x200pxartboard andsetthestroke widthto1.5pt. Toachieve ahand-drawn appearance,chooseorganicshapes overexcessively geometric ones.However,its essentialweensure thatvectorpointsaresmooth,and thefinalartworkappearsclean,devoid ofany unnaturalbumpsorirregularitiesinthestrokes.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:52354370-65f2-42c4-9a77-c5c04e8d229f"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:2300f52e-fccb-497f-936d-8c6e076c5695", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Strokewidth", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2300f52e-fccb-497f-936d-8c6e076c5695", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Thestrokewidthremains at1.5ptwitha consistent widthprofile.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nStrokesetuponillustration\n\nMake sureyou configure the strokefunctionsin AdobeIllustratortomatchtheparametersoutlined intheseguidelines.\n\nDon't mix stroke widths in an illustration.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:baeeddfc-1cbb-4d0f-a823-a2b6a91fbef8"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:7cec23ed-9d82-46a7-8fa1-bdbf762e7055", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "FilledAreas", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "7cec23ed-9d82-46a7-8fa1-bdbf762e7055", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Somepartsof theStandalone should haveup to2filled areas.These areas shouldrepresent5-15%of the full illustrations tomaintaina goodbalancebetween outlinesand filled areas and to ensure consistency acrosstheillustrations.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nThefilled area mustnotexceed 15%oftheillustration.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:b4324906-4a83-47ce-a494-f070e9735629"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:164c7cbd-6a70-4cd4-9568-6c16e0a07916", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Crossinglines", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "164c7cbd-6a70-4cd4-9568-6c16e0a07916", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Whensuitablefortheillustration,employa'crossing line'toenhanceit.Thismethod involvesincorporating anorganiclinethatintersectstheartwork,adding dynamismandengagement.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:d16b55f6-43dd-4b83-accf-3c2d49992723"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:145baaeb-8471-48de-8f21-94c58ebc3c24", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Eyesandexpression", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "145baaeb-8471-48de-8f21-94c58ebc3c24", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Toinfuseourillustrationswith awarmeraesthetic,depicthuman and animaleyesina morerealisticway.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:c15dadd5-42e6-4bbe-8f06-d0c8e88bc773"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:ff272388-af15-4254-83f6-02c8d8b2730f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Humaneyes", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "ff272388-af15-4254-83f6-02c8d8b2730f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Forhuman eyes,we emphasizedetail whenrendering theuppereyelid and eyeball.The shape of theupper eyelid mayvarybased onthesubject'scharacteristics,likeageand ethnicity.\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:eddd2fb0-f4a8-4964-a1e1-c5fc8b9e7567"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:2f902942-1cbe-4110-9370-c930fa441d08", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Aniimaleyes", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "2f902942-1cbe-4110-9370-c930fa441d08", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Wemeticulouslydesign animaleyestocapturetheessenceofeachspecies,showingavarietyofeyeshapes androundnesswhilestrivingforarealistic,handcraftedappearance. Wedon'tuseperfectcirclesandinsteadoptforamorenatural shapethatbetterrepresentstheiractual appearance.\n\n<!-- image -->\n\nColor combination\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:afa37476-f601-4a30-a583-7cd996d43e6b"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:de6234ae-3a52-48d3-b3b6-22e32ebbd8cb", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_title": "Stroke features", "section_type": "heading", "page_number": 9, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "de6234ae-3a52-48d3-b3b6-22e32ebbd8cb", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "Thecorners and capsof the strokesshould always\n\nhaveroundedattributes.", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:4a42160b-3e44-4a61-bccb-9ed21bf52371"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:8eafa85d-fe4f-4030-a68d-a9bc3ebc91d8", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 10, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "8eafa85d-fe4f-4030-a68d-a9bc3ebc91d8", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file_name": "BI Design Style Guide 1.pdf", "source_document_id": "3a3871a8-b21d-44c3-883b-299017d57793", "text": "ILLUSTRATIONS DESIGN GUIDE\n\nBoehringer Ingelheim ILLUSTRATIONS DESIGN GUIDE\n\n<!-- image -->\n\n<!-- image -->", "SECTION_HAS_CHUNK": [{"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:chunk:d4512ebb-b151-409a-861e-f2291aa22494"}]}, {"@id": "urn:kg:boehringer-ingelheim:section:7d000c79-d3f0-4d14-8a0f-e7085b25ad6f", "@type": "Section", "graphScope": "brand", "section_type": "body", "page_number": 11, "source_document_type": "brand_book", "section_id": "7d000c79-d3f0-4d14-8a0f-e7085b25ad6f", "extraction_method": "docling", "source_file